{"hw":"σῴζω","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">σῴζω</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">σῴζω</span>, with <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ι</span> wherever <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ζ</span> follows <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ω</span>, as <span class=\"gk\">σῴζω</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">EM</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">741.27</span> </span>, and so (written <span class=\"gk\">σωιζ-</span>) in Inscrr. and Papyri down to <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">iii B.C.</span>, e.g. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">12.625.4</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">22.687.35</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1611.378</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Isyll.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">75</span> </span> (lapis), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">PCair.Zen.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">482.17</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">532.23</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(iii B.C.)</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Test.Epict.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.6</span> </span> <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">(iii/ii B.C.)</span>, (<span class=\"lex-etym gk\">ἀνα-</span>) <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">22.492.13</span> </span>, also in cod. Laur. of <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">El.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">993</span> </span>, al., but otherwise without it, e.g. <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἔσωσε</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9(2).257.11</sp